# ChatGPT Obsidian Memory

Long-term chat memory captured from ChatGPT (paste or browser extension) lives in the Obsidian vault folder `ChatGPT-Memory/`.

When the user asks you to recall prior decisions, preferences, designs, or chat context:

1. Search and read notes under `ChatGPT-Memory/` (including `Index.md`).
2. Prefer those notes over guessing.
3. Cite the note filename (e.g. `05-10-2026-Some-Topic.md`) when you use it.

Do not call any ChatGPT / OpenAI API for this memory. Cursor only reads the local vault files.
